<Base title="Agentic AI | Kubernautic"><section class="shell page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">INTELLIGENCE / WITH GUARDRAILS</span><h1>AI that informs.<br/><span class="gradient-text">Humans that decide.</span></h1><p>Our guiding design principle: turn raw Kubernetes signals into meaningful context and explainable recommendations while preserving operator control.</p></section><section class="shell section single-section"><div class="steps"><div class="step"><span>01 / OBSERVE</span><h3>Collect signals</h3><p>Events, workload health, metrics and relevant cluster context.</p></div><div class="step"><span>02 / REASON</span><h3>Investigate</h3><p>Relate symptoms, changes and possible causes.</p></div><div class="step"><span>03 / RECOMMEND</span><h3>Explain next steps</h3><p>Show options and their reasoning in the context of the incident.</p></div><div class="step"><span>04 / GOVERN</span><h3>Stay in control</h3><p>Make policy, approval and an audit trail prerequisites to action.</p></div></div></section><section class="dark-section section"><div class="shell note-panel"><div><span class="eyebrow">READ-ONLY DEMO FIRST</span><h2>Explore the intelligence without executing changes.</h2><p>The first public preview is intended for learning and evaluation. It will not expose write operations or autonomous remediation to registered visitors.</p></div><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/console/">Console Preview ↗</a></div></section><CTA/></Base>
